<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Portuguese (Portugal) — the app's default language. This is the fallback for
     every phone whose language is not English, unless a language is pinned in
     Settings (English lives in values-en).

     Copy rules for this file (please keep them when editing):
       • Never write "comprimido(s)". Use the `unit_pill` plurals below — the
         stored default label in `unit_pill_default` is only a marker that
         `util/Units.kt` swaps for the right singular/plural at render time.
       • Quote with “ ” (never straight \" quotes) so it reads like Portuguese
         typography and stays consistent across screens.
       • Errors are instructions ("Indique…"), never a repeat of the field label.
       • One term per concept: "idioma" (not "língua"), "toma" for a dose.
       • Impersonal, calm voice — no "nós"/"podemos" first person.
       • Keep labels on narrow controls short; long text is what gets clipped. -->
